<title>JAPAN: Nisshin, Hanwa and Mitsui in China steel venture.</title>
<headline>Nisshin, Hanwa and Mitsui in China steel venture.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nisshin Steel Co Ltd, Hanwa Co Ltd and Mitsui &amp; Co Ltd plan to take a total 34 percent share in a venture to build a cold-rolled stainless steel plant in China, Nisshin said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>The Chinese side will take the remaining stake, Nisshin said in a statement.</p>
<p>Investment in the plant, which will produce 80,000 tonnes of stainless steel per year, would be $150 million, it said.</p>
<p>Operations at the plant are scheduled to begin in September 1998.</p>
<p>The company did not provide further details.</p>
</text>
